-- title:
--   Finite contact quotients as products of truncated polynomial algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $g_2,g_3\in\mathbb C$, let $A=\mathbb C[t,x_1,x_2,x_3]$, and choose either of the elliptic-extension chart derivations
--
--   $$D_0=\partial_t+x_2\partial_{x_1}+(6x_1^2-g_2/2)\partial_{x_2}-x_1\partial_{x_3},$$
--
--   $$D_1=\partial_t+(-6x_2^2+(g_2/2)x_1^2)\partial_{x_1}+(-1/2-g_2x_1x_2-(3g_3/2)x_1^2)\partial_{x_2}+(-2g_2x_2^2-3g_3x_1x_2)\partial_{x_3}.$$
--
--   Write $D=D_c$. For each $v\in\mathbb C^4$ and $n\in\mathbb N$, let $C(v,n)$ be the chart contact ideal generated by polynomials whose first $n$ $D$-jets vanish at $v$.
--
--   Let $V\subseteq\mathbb C^4$ be any finite set and assign an order $n_v\in\mathbb N$ to each $v\in V$. Then there exists an isomorphism of complex algebras
--
--   $$A\Big/\bigcap_{v\in V}C(v,n_v)\ \cong_{\mathbb C}\ \prod_{v\in V}\mathbb C[T]\big/\big((T-v_0)^{n_v}\big).$$
--
--   This identifies the full quotient algebra, including its multiplication and scalar action, with a product of translated truncated polynomial algebras. At a positive order $n_v$, the local parameter $T-v_0$ is nilpotent of order $n_v$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The result is unconditional for the defined chart derivations and contact ideals. It uses the already proved contact structure and bounded Hermite interpolation theorems. Hermite interpolation is applied separately at each singleton point, so distinct full coordinate vectors may have the same first coordinate. No global first-coordinate injectivity, time-presentation, finite-dimensionality, nonsingularity or chart-cubic hypothesis is assumed. Zero orders and empty $V$ are included: an order-zero factor is the zero algebra and an empty product is the zero algebra, matching the quotient by the whole ring. The formal statement asserts existence of a complex algebra isomorphism; it does not specify its coordinate action. The chart indices 0 and 1 correspond to the homogeneous-coordinate charts $S_0$ and $S_2$. This is a finite local algebra calculation, with no global degree or algebraic-group estimate.
-- source:
--   Derived finite local algebra model for the commutative-algebra approach associated with Senthil Kumar K (2026), Appendix A, https://doi.org/10.1017/S001309152610145X. Uses the proved contact structure and bounded Hermite interpolation theorems. At each point, the time-polynomial evaluation map onto the contact quotient is surjective by singleton Hermite interpolation and has kernel generated by (T-v_0)^n. The first isomorphism theorem and the Chinese remainder theorem give the complex algebra product. This is not quoted as Theorem A.2. Primary formal references: Derivation.comp_aeval_eq, Polynomial.X_sub_C_pow_dvd_iff, Polynomial.factorial_smul_hasseDeriv, Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective, Ideal.quotientInfRingEquivPiQuotient and AlgEquiv.piCongrRight.

